:Namespace MICROGPT
⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⍝ microgpt.apln — array-native port of karpathy/microgpt
⍝ Full-sequence forward: (n × NE) matrices throughout, causal mask
⍝ instead of per-token dispatch, multi-head attention via ⍤2.
⍝ No KV cache during training. Companion to microgpt_kv.apln.
⍝ ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

⎕IO←0 ⋄ ⎕FR←645 ⋄ ⎕PP←17 ⋄ ⎕CT←0

NE ← 16 ⋄ BLK ← 16 ⋄ NH ← 4 ⋄ HD ← 4 ⋄ VS ← 27 ⋄ BOSID ← 26
EPSR ← 1E¯5

⍝ optimizer + training hyperparameters (match microgpt.py)
LR0        ← 0.01
B1         ← 0.85
B2         ← 0.99
EPSA       ← 1E¯8
NSTEPS_FULL ← 1000

⍝ weight matrix names, used for Adam iteration and gradient accumulation
NAMES ← 'wte' 'wpe' 'lm_head' 'attn_wq' 'attn_wk' 'attn_wv' 'attn_wo' 'mlp_fc1' 'mlp_fc2'

W    ← ⎕NS''
G    ← ⎕NS''
ACT  ← ⎕NS''
OPT  ← ⎕NS''
DATA ← ⎕NS''

⍝ Row-wise primitives (apply via ⍤1 over the last axis)
rmsnorm ← {⍵÷(EPSR+(+/⍵*2)÷≢⍵)*0.5}
softmax ← {e÷+/e←*⍵-⌈/⍵}
relu    ← 0∘⌈

⍝ Gradient primitives (row-wise via ⍤1). See apl_research_dossier.md for derivations.
⍝   rmsnorm:  y = x/rms  →  dx = (dy - y·mean(y·dy))/rms
⍝   softmax:  p = softmax(s) → ds = p·(dp - ⟨p,dp⟩)   (Jacobian-vector product)
rmsnorm_bwd ← { dy←⍺ ⋄ x←⍵
    rms ← (EPSR+(+/x*2)÷≢x)*0.5
    y   ← x÷rms
    (dy-y×(+/y×dy)÷≢y)÷rms
}
softmax_bwd ← { p←⍺ ⋄ dy←⍵ ⋄ p×dy-+/p×dy }

loadmat ← {
    tn ← ⍵ ⎕NTIE 0
    v  ← ⎕NREAD tn 645 (×/⍺) 0
    _  ← ⎕NUNTIE tn
    ⍺ ⍴ v
}

LOAD ← {dir←⍵
    W.wte     ← (VS NE)     loadmat dir,'/wte.bin'
    W.wpe     ← (BLK NE)    loadmat dir,'/wpe.bin'
    W.lm_head ← (VS NE)     loadmat dir,'/lm_head.bin'
    W.attn_wq ← (NE NE)     loadmat dir,'/attn_wq.bin'
    W.attn_wk ← (NE NE)     loadmat dir,'/attn_wk.bin'
    W.attn_wv ← (NE NE)     loadmat dir,'/attn_wv.bin'
    W.attn_wo ← (NE NE)     loadmat dir,'/attn_wo.bin'
    W.mlp_fc1 ← ((4×NE) NE) loadmat dir,'/mlp_fc1.bin'
    W.mlp_fc2 ← (NE (4×NE)) loadmat dir,'/mlp_fc2.bin'
    ⍬
}

⍝ Additive causal mask: 0 where j ≤ i, -1E10 where j > i.
MASK ← {¯1E10×~(⍳⍵)∘.≥⍳⍵}

⍝ --- full-sequence forward (n × NE matrices throughout) ---
⍝ ⍵: integer token id vector. Returns (n × VS) logits.
⍝ Caches every intermediate in ACT for the backward pass.
FWD ← { ids←⍵
    n  ← ≢ids
    X  ← W.wte[ids;] + W.wpe[⍳n;]
    Xp ← rmsnorm⍤1⊢X                            ⍝ primes residual stream
    X1 ← rmsnorm⍤1⊢Xp                           ⍝ pre-attention norm
    Q  ← X1 +.× ⍉W.attn_wq
    K  ← X1 +.× ⍉W.attn_wk
    V  ← X1 +.× ⍉W.attn_wv
    ⍝ split heads: (n NE) → (n NH HD) → transpose to (NH n HD)
    Qh ← 1 0 2⍉(n,NH,HD)⍴Q
    Kh ← 1 0 2⍉(n,NH,HD)⍴K
    Vh ← 1 0 2⍉(n,NH,HD)⍴V
    ⍝ scaled dot-product scores + causal mask (broadcast over heads via ⍤2)
    S  ← (MASK n)+⍤2⊢(Qh +.×⍤2⊢⍉⍤2⊢Kh)÷HD*0.5
    A  ← softmax⍤1⊢S
    H  ← A +.×⍤2⊢Vh
    ⍝ concat heads: (NH n HD) → (n NH HD) → ravel inner 2 axes
    Hc ← ,⍤2⊢1 0 2⍉H
    X2 ← Xp + Hc +.× ⍉W.attn_wo                 ⍝ residual
    X3 ← rmsnorm⍤1⊢X2
    M0 ← X3 +.× ⍉W.mlp_fc1
    Mr ← relu M0
    X4 ← X2 + Mr +.× ⍉W.mlp_fc2                 ⍝ residual
    logits ← X4 +.× ⍉W.lm_head
    ACT.ids ← ids
    ACT.X ← X ⋄ ACT.Xp ← Xp ⋄ ACT.X1 ← X1
    ACT.Q ← Q ⋄ ACT.K ← K ⋄ ACT.V ← V
    ACT.Qh ← Qh ⋄ ACT.Kh ← Kh ⋄ ACT.Vh ← Vh
    ACT.S ← S ⋄ ACT.A ← A ⋄ ACT.H ← H ⋄ ACT.Hc ← Hc
    ACT.X2 ← X2 ⋄ ACT.X3 ← X3 ⋄ ACT.M0 ← M0 ⋄ ACT.Mr ← Mr ⋄ ACT.X4 ← X4
    ACT.logits ← logits
    logits
}

⍝ --- full-sequence backward pass ---
⍝ ⍵: target token ids (length n). Uses ACT from the most recent FWD call.
⍝ Populates G.* with gradients mirroring W.*. Returns mean cross-entropy loss.
BWD ← { targets←⍵
    n ← ≢targets

    ⍝ softmax + cross-entropy combined: dlogits = (probs - onehot) / n
    P         ← softmax⍤1⊢ACT.logits
    onehot    ← targets ∘.= ⍳VS
    p_target  ← +/P×onehot                          ⍝ (n,) probability at each target
    loss      ← -(÷n)×+/⍟p_target
    dlogits   ← (P-onehot)÷n

    ⍝ final linear: logits = X4 @ lm_head.T
    G.lm_head ← (⍉dlogits)+.×ACT.X4
    dX4       ← dlogits+.×W.lm_head

    ⍝ MLP block (residual: X4 = X2 + Mr @ mlp_fc2.T)
    G.mlp_fc2 ← (⍉dX4)+.×ACT.Mr
    dMr       ← dX4+.×W.mlp_fc2
    dM0       ← dMr×ACT.M0>0                        ⍝ relu backward
    G.mlp_fc1 ← (⍉dM0)+.×ACT.X3
    dX3       ← dM0+.×W.mlp_fc1

    ⍝ rmsnorm backward X2 → X3
    dX2_mlp ← dX3 (rmsnorm_bwd⍤1) ACT.X2
    dX2     ← dX4+dX2_mlp                           ⍝ residual merge

    ⍝ attention output projection (residual: X2 = Xp + Hc @ attn_wo.T)
    G.attn_wo ← (⍉dX2)+.×ACT.Hc
    dHc       ← dX2+.×W.attn_wo
    dXp_res   ← dX2                                  ⍝ residual path for Xp

    ⍝ un-concat heads: (n NE) → (n NH HD) → (NH n HD)
    dH ← 1 0 2⍉(n,NH,HD)⍴dHc

    ⍝ per-head: H = A @ Vh  →  dA = dH @ Vh.T ,  dVh = A.T @ dH
    dVh ← (⍉⍤2⊢ACT.A)+.×⍤2⊢dH
    dA  ← dH+.×⍤2⊢⍉⍤2⊢ACT.Vh

    ⍝ softmax backward per-row over the last axis of (NH n n)
    dS_masked ← ACT.A (softmax_bwd⍤1) dA

    ⍝ mask is additive, scale is ÷sqrt(HD), so dS_raw = dS_masked / sqrt(HD)
    dS_raw ← dS_masked÷HD*0.5

    ⍝ per-head: S_raw = Qh @ Kh.T  →  dQh = dS @ Kh ,  dKh = dS.T @ Qh
    dQh ← dS_raw+.×⍤2⊢ACT.Kh
    dKh ← (⍉⍤2⊢dS_raw)+.×⍤2⊢ACT.Qh

    ⍝ merge heads back: (NH n HD) → (n NH HD) → (n NE)
    dQ ← (n,NE)⍴1 0 2⍉dQh
    dK ← (n,NE)⍴1 0 2⍉dKh
    dV ← (n,NE)⍴1 0 2⍉dVh

    ⍝ linear backward for Q/K/V projections (all read X1 as input)
    G.attn_wq ← (⍉dQ)+.×ACT.X1
    G.attn_wk ← (⍉dK)+.×ACT.X1
    G.attn_wv ← (⍉dV)+.×ACT.X1
    dX1       ← (dQ+.×W.attn_wq)+(dK+.×W.attn_wk)+(dV+.×W.attn_wv)

    ⍝ rmsnorm backward Xp → X1, merge with residual from attn_wo path
    dXp ← dXp_res + dX1 (rmsnorm_bwd⍤1) ACT.Xp

    ⍝ rmsnorm backward X → Xp
    dX ← dXp (rmsnorm_bwd⍤1) ACT.X

    ⍝ scatter-add into wte (non-unique indices via onehot-matmul)
    G.wte ← (⍉ACT.ids∘.=⍳VS)+.×dX

    ⍝ wpe: each position index unique, dense copy into rows 0..n-1
    G.wpe ← (BLK,NE)⍴0
    G.wpe[⍳n;] ← dX

    loss
}

⍝ --- Adam optimizer state init ---
⍝ Creates OPT.m and OPT.v as namespaces with one zero buffer per weight matrix.
⍝ Every ⍎ side-effect is bound to _ so the inner dfn does not return early
⍝ on the first bare expression (Dyalog dfn quirk).
INIT_OPT ← {
    OPT.m ← ⎕NS''
    OPT.v ← ⎕NS''
    _ ← {name←⍵
        shp ← ⍴W⍎name
        _ ← ⍎'OPT.m.',name,' ← shp⍴0'
        _ ← ⍎'OPT.v.',name,' ← shp⍴0'
        ⍬
    }¨NAMES
    ⍬
}

⍝ --- one Adam step ---
⍝ ⍵: (step, lr). step is 0-indexed. Updates W in place using G and OPT.m/OPT.v.
⍝ Standard Adam with bias correction, matches microgpt.py's loop body.
⍝ Locals are named mom1/mom2/etc. to avoid shadowing namespace member
⍝ access like OPT.m / OPT.v (Dyalog parses the bare `v` as a local).
ADAM_STEP ← { step lr←⍵
    t   ← step+1
    bc1 ← 1-B1*t
    bc2 ← 1-B2*t
    _ ← {name←⍵
        grad  ← G⍎name
        mom1  ← (B1×OPT.m⍎name)+(1-B1)×grad
        mom2  ← (B2×OPT.v⍎name)+(1-B2)×grad*2
        m_hat ← mom1÷bc1
        v_hat ← mom2÷bc2
        w_new ← (W⍎name)-lr×m_hat÷EPSA+v_hat*0.5
        _ ← ⍎'W.',name,' ← w_new'
        _ ← ⍎'OPT.m.',name,' ← mom1'
        _ ← ⍎'OPT.v.',name,' ← mom2'
        ⍬
    }¨NAMES
    ⍬
}

⍝ --- one training step ---
⍝ ⍵: (input_token_ids, target_token_ids, step_index). Runs FWD+BWD+ADAM_STEP.
⍝ Returns the loss for this step.
TRAIN_STEP ← { inputs targets step←⍵
    _ ← FWD inputs
    l ← BWD targets
    lr ← LR0×1-step÷NSTEPS_FULL
    _ ← ADAM_STEP step lr
    l
}

⍝ --- data loading + tokenizer ---
⍝ ⍵: path to the dataset text file (one document per line).
⍝ Populates DATA namespace with docs, uchars, encode, decode, BOS token id.
INIT_DATA ← { path←⍵
    DATA.docs   ← (⊂'')~⍨⊃⎕NGET path 1
    uniq        ← ∪∊DATA.docs
    DATA.uchars ← uniq[⍋uniq]
    DATA.BOSID  ← ≢DATA.uchars
    DATA.VS     ← 1+≢DATA.uchars
    ⍬
}

⍝ Encode/decode live in the MICROGPT namespace so their lexical scope can
⍝ see DATA. If stored as members of DATA the dfns fail to resolve DATA at
⍝ call time (their home namespace would be DATA, not MICROGPT).
encode ← {DATA.uchars⍳⍵}
decode ← {DATA.uchars[⍵]}

⍝ --- full training loop ---
⍝ ⍵: number of steps. Uses DATA.docs in shuffled order.
⍝ Returns the vector of per-step losses.
TRAIN ← { nsteps←⍵
    shuffled ← DATA.docs[(≢DATA.docs)?(≢DATA.docs)]
    _ ← INIT_OPT ⍬
    losses ← nsteps⍴0
    step ← 0
    _ ← {
        doc ← ((≢shuffled)|step)⊃shuffled            ⍝ A|B is B mod A in APL
        tokens ← DATA.BOSID,(encode doc),DATA.BOSID
        n ← BLK⌊¯1+≢tokens
        inputs  ← n↑tokens
        targets ← n↑1↓tokens
        l ← TRAIN_STEP inputs targets step
        losses[step] ← l
        step +← 1
        ⍬
    }¨⍳nsteps
    losses
}

⍝ --- inference: sample one name ---
⍝ ⍵: temperature (0, 1]. Returns a character vector (without BOS).
⍝ Re-runs FWD on the growing sequence each step (no KV cache; BLK is small).
GEN ← { temp←⍵
    step ← {
        (1<≢⍵)∧(DATA.BOSID=⊃⌽⍵): ⍵                   ⍝ stop if last token is BOS
        logits   ← FWD ⍵
        last_row ← logits[(¯1+≢logits);]              ⍝ length-VS logit vector
        p        ← softmax last_row÷temp
        next     ← ⊃⍸(+\p)≥?0                         ⍝ inverse-CDF sampling
        ⍵,next
    }
    ids  ← step⍣BLK⊢,DATA.BOSID                      ⍝ at most BLK tokens
    body ← 1↓ids                                      ⍝ strip leading BOS
    body ← (body⍳DATA.BOSID)↑body                     ⍝ truncate at first BOS
    decode body
}

:EndNamespace
